# The closed schema of the lockers kiosk's ViewState canonical form (T2G5), written from apps/lockers/lkrx/vstate/vstate.h of business-apps
# (its "CANONICAL FORM" and its enums: LKS_*, LK_NK_*, LK_DISMISS_*, LK_PH_*, LK_DOOR_*, LK_BANNER_*, the bounds of "Bounds") and the rules of
# docs/lockers/ui-rules.md. This is the product's file to own: the gate parses it with ui_schema_parse and knows no field name of it.
# [V] the texts of the fault enum are `lk_fault_name` of lk/types: check them against the product before this file is used for a grade.
enum screen splash welcome choose opened shift report lockout fault_storage fault_relay
enum lang bg en
enum nkind dialog banner snackbar
enum dismiss overlay banner_not_saved banner_audit banner_sync banner_codes_offline banner_codes_stale banner_self_test
enum bannerid not_saved audit sync codes_offline codes_stale self_test
enum phrase reject_invalid reject_unknown reject_codes_unavailable no_locker fault saved not_saved audit sync_rejected sync_late codes_offline codes_stale self_test
enum fault relay_busy kiosk_busy lock_unavailable relay_safety_stop relay_offline relay_error storage_error codes_unavailable book_rejected locker_missing
enum door nothing_opened maybe_opened opened

object sizeitem
  field size uint 5
  field free uint 65535
end

# The arguments of a phrase: the keys of its case, in the order of vstate.h; every other phrase has `{}`.
object args
  switch @ phrase
  on fault
  field fault enum fault
  field door enum door
  field locker uint 999 null
  on sync_rejected
  field status uint 65535
  on sync_late
  field hour uint 23
  field minute uint 59
  on codes_offline
  field hour uint 23
  field minute uint 59
  on self_test
  field issues uint 4095
  endswitch
end

object notice
  field kind enum nkind
  field dismiss enum dismiss
  field phrase enum phrase
  field args obj args by phrase
  field warning bool
  field countdown_ms uint 300000 null
end

object banner
  field id enum bannerid
  field phrase enum phrase
  field args obj args by phrase
  field warning bool
end

object view
  field screen enum screen
  field lang enum lang
  field countdown_ms uint 300000 null
  switch screen
  on welcome
  field pad_len uint 64
  on choose
  field sizes list sizeitem 6
  on opened
  field locker uint 999
  field first_time bool
  on shift
  field done uint 65535
  field total uint 65535
  on report
  field released uint 65535
  field ok uint 65535
  field faults uint 65535
  field write_failed bool
  on fault_storage
  field fault enum fault
  on fault_relay
  field fault enum fault
  endswitch
  field notice obj notice null
  field banners list banner 6
end

top view
role screen view screen
role lang view lang
role notice view notice
role banners view banners
role n_kind notice kind
role n_dismiss notice dismiss
role n_phrase notice phrase
role n_countdown notice countdown_ms
role b_id banner id
role b_phrase banner phrase

# A banner's dismiss intent is implied by its id (vstate.h, lk_banner_t).
bannerdismiss not_saved banner_not_saved
bannerdismiss audit banner_audit
bannerdismiss sync banner_sync
bannerdismiss codes_offline banner_codes_offline
bannerdismiss codes_stale banner_codes_stale
bannerdismiss self_test banner_self_test

# A message that is a screen has no place in the closed schema: these keys name one.
forbid message text title detail

idle welcome
lang_default bg
# Dialogs and snackbars clear on their own (their countdown); a banner does not (docs/lockers/ui-rules.md, "Screen timers").
expiring dialog snackbar
